president Trump's former campaign  manager is still facing charges filed by  Special Counsel Robert Muller a federal  judge did not dismiss the indictment of  Paul Manafort but he was skeptical of  mowers authority in the case Jeff Pegues  has more on the hearing in Alexandria  Virginia and the president's reaction to  it to which on on Friday President Trump  seized on the judges words as evidence  that the special counsels investigation  had gone too far  judge questions Muller's authority to  prosecute manifold former Trump campaign  Chairman Paul Manafort was indicted by  the special counsel on bank fraud  charges in connection to his alleged  activities predating the 2016 election  but during a court hearing Friday US  District Judge TS Ellis wondered whether  in pursuing the case against mana for  special counsel Robert Muller had  exceeded his mandate to investigate  Russian election interference Ellis said  the special counsel was trying to  tighten the screws on mana for in order  to force him to testify against the  president you don't really care about Mr  Man affords bank fraud what you really  care about is what information mr. mana  fort can give you that would reflect on  mr. Trump or lead to his prosecution or  impeachment but Deputy Solicitor General  Michael Dreeben who represented Muller's  office during the hearing responded we  take very seriously the primary mission  that was assigned to us well the  president praised the judge and used his  comments to rally supporters against the  Russia investigation it is unclear what  kind of effect the judges comments will  actually have on the special counsels  investigation and the special counsels  case against Paul Manafort attorneys who  have faced judge Ellis in the past say  that his comments are not always a  reflection of how he will actually rule  for CBS this morning Saturday Jeff  Pegues Washington
 

